  "tagline": "CNCF multi-tenant, horizontally scalable long-term storage for Prometheus metrics on object storage.",
  "description": "Cortex is the original horizontally scalable, multi-tenant Prometheus backend, started at Weaveworks in 2016 and now a CNCF incubating project. Prometheus servers or agents remote-write into distributors, ingesters batch samples into TSDB blocks on object storage, and queriers and store-gateways answer PromQL across tenants with per-tenant limits, a ruler and an Alertmanager. Grafana Mimir forked from it in 2022, but Cortex continues under vendor-neutral Apache-2.0 governance, with recent releases adding a Parquet mode for store-gateways and Prometheus remote write 2.0. Choose it when you want Mimir-style architecture without AGPL.",
